{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Streaming Speech-to-Speech \u2014 Moshi, Hibiki, and Full-Duplex Dialogue Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: the interface"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Moshi exposes a WebSocket server that takes 80 ms chunks of Mimi-encoded audio and returns 80 ms chunks of Mimi-encoded audio. Both ways. Constantly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import asyncio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import websockets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from moshi.client_utils import encode_audio_mimi, decode_audio_mimi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "async def moshi_chat():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    async with websockets.connect(\"ws://localhost:8998/api/chat\") as ws:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mic_task = asyncio.create_task(stream_mic_to(ws))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spk_task = asyncio.create_task(stream_from_to_speaker(ws))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        await asyncio.gather(mic_task, spk_task)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: the full-duplex loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "async def stream_mic_to(ws):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    async for chunk_80ms in mic_stream_at_12_5_hz():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mimi_tokens = encode_audio_mimi(chunk_80ms)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        await ws.send(serialize(mimi_tokens))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "async def stream_from_to_speaker(ws):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    async for msg in ws:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mimi_tokens, text_token = deserialize(msg)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        audio = decode_audio_mimi(mimi_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        await play(audio)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Both directions run simultaneously. Python asyncio or Rust futures are the standard transport."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: the training objective (conceptual)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For every 80 ms frame `t`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Input: `user_mimi[0..t]`, `moshi_mimi[0..t-1]`, `moshi_text[0..t-1]`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Predict: `moshi_text[t]`, then `moshi_mimi[t, codebook_0..7]`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Text is predicted before audio (inner monologue); audio is predicted codebook-sequential within the depth transformer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: where Moshi wins and where it doesn't"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Moshi wins:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Sub-250 ms end-to-end on cheap hardware."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Natural back-channels and interruptions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- No pipeline glue code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Moshi does not win:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Tool calling (not trained for it; you need a separate LLM path)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Long reasoning (Moshi is an 8B-ish dialogue model, not Claude/GPT-4)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Factual accuracy on niche topics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Most production enterprise use cases (still use pipelines in 2026)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. It simulates the two-stream + inner-monologue architecture symbolically.\n2. **Medium.** Pull Moshi from HuggingFace, run the server, test one conversation. Measure wall-clock latency from end-of-user-speech to start-of-Moshi-response.\n3. **Hard.** Take your Lesson 12 pipeline agent and compare P50 latency vs Moshi on 20 matched test utterances. Write up when a pipeline architecturally wins anyway."
      ]
    }
  ],
